1
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:12,100
The white night is burning,
and so are the steel masses.

5
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? You get it, you get it.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,480
Once you understand,
follow me without a word.

8
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,900
Ryo-san,
you're going to become a millionaire!

9
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:50,320
The sky is blue,
and what a refreshing day it is.

10
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
On a day like this, something good might...

11
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,180
Doesn't seem likely, does it.

12
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:03,960
Hungry!

13
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:08,060
Drink some water and quiet that stomach of yours,
you idiot!

14
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,480
Chief!

15
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,720
Good morning.

16
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,780
Chief.

17
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,140
I don't know anything about it.

18
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,020
Really?

19
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:22,000
You'll just blow your salary
on horse racing and pachinko,

20
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,880
and then come asking me
to lend you money, right?

21
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,080
Wow, you've got me all figured out.

22
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,760
As expected of you, Chief.

23
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:30,560
Hmph, it's all written right on your face.

24
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,100
On that dopey face of yours.

25
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,200
Dopey face.

26
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,520
That's right. Listen, Ryotsu.

27
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,480
With the salary you
receive as a police officer,

28
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,940
You should be able to get
by just fine on your own.

29
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:47,920
Stop chasing easy money through gambling and shady side jobs,
and save steadily instead.

30
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,720
What I spend my money on is my own business,
isn't it?

31
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,840
Mind your own business.

32
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,360
What a hopeless guy.

33
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:01,940
Easier said than done, but I'm starving.

34
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:06,060
A gift from the gods!

35
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:08,200
Hey, hey, officer!

36
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,480
That's mine, you know. I dropped it.

37
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,240
What?

38
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:17,040
Well, there's no choice.

39
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:22,200
You're hungry?

40
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,400
Then come over to my place.

41
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:39,140
I can finally breathe again.

42
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:43,620
This yard is huge, though.

43
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:48,320
Doesn't look like it, but our place
is the biggest mansion around here.

44
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:52,700
With a yard this big,
cleaning it alone would be a lot of work.

45
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,680
What are you going to do with that?

46
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:58,360
I was thinking of digging a hole
in the backyard for dumping trash.

47
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,720
Alright, I'll do it for you.

48
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:02,380
Around here?

49
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,540
Thanks.

50
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:08,000
Sure thing, my belly's full now,
so it's an easy job.

51
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,765
Well then,

52
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:12,240
I'll be over there watching
a flower arrangement video.

53
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,460
Leave it to me.

54
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,220
What's this?

55
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,460
It's a koban!

56
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,620
Just kidding, it's probably a toy anyway.

57
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,780
The world isn't that sweet.

58
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:50,240
Could this actually be real?

59
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:51,780
Ugh!

60
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,080
Ugh!

61
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:53,780
Ugh!

62
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:54,160
Ugh!

63
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,680
Officer.

64
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,280
Thanks for your hard work.

65
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,740
The tea's ready.

66
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:01,000
Come over here and take a break.

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,180
No, I'm good.

68
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:03,780
I hate tea.

69
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:05,940
I'm the type who falls
apart if I take a break.

70
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,100
Never mind.

71
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:10,280
I'm still in the middle of work, you see.

72
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,720
Really?

73
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:12,960
Phew.

74
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:16,040
This isn't like a 500-yen coin, you know.

75
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,960
Ryotsu?

76
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:17,340
Good!

77
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:18,900
C-Chief!

78
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,760
What are you doing over there?

79
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:24,040
No, well, it's nothing really...

80
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:27,060
That flustered look of yours is suspicious.

81
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,660
You, you're hiding something, aren't you?

82
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:35,800
Come on, I'm not hiding anything at all.

83
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,540
What's this?

84
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,880
Th-that's a koban!

85
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:43,820
G-geez, looks like it.

86
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,020
She's not my mother!

87
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,500
Grandma, Grandma.

88
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:52,120
A gold koban came out of your garden.

89
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,240
A gold koban?

90
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,700
Damn it, I'm the one who found it!

91
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,740
So the gold koban belongs to the old lady?

92
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:07,000
It can't be helped, Ryo-chan.

93
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,040
It was definitely buried by
the road crew guy's ancestor.

94
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,840
There was a note, after all.

95
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,920
You're being a poor sport.

96
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:16,060
Just give up quietly, won't you.

97
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:17,200
That's right.

98
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:20,660
Just feeling the gold koban
is enough to make me happy.

99
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:35,320
Is Lord Ryotsu in?

100
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:36,820
L-lord?

101
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:40,040
Ryotsu is right here.

102
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,060
Are you here to help with the digging again?

103
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,560
Is that your specialty?

104
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,880
Regarding this matter,

105
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,480
Lord Ryotsu's exploits

106
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,320
were truly magnificent.

107
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,940
Even your way of speaking has changed.

108
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:55,900
You've become quite refined.

109
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:58,480
So, from the road construction office,

110
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,220
I have brought a reward for Lord Ryotsu.

111
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:03,720
Do not hesitate to accept it.

112
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:09,160
Well then, farewell, indeed.

113
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,960
I was surprised by that substitute.

114
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:20,880
What, you said it was a reward,
but there's only one sheet in here!

115
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,960
What a stingy bunch, honestly.

116
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:26,180
Don't complain when you've been
given something by someone else.

117
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,880
What, it's just one scrap of paper!

118
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,280
This is called a kogitte.

119
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:38,620
1,101,001,000 man, 100,000, 1,000,000

120
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,600
The groom is getting here early.

121
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:43,260
Ten million.

122
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:45,700
One hundred million yen.

123
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,460
One hundred million yen.

124
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,320
One hundred million yen, is it?

125
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:51,000
Ryo-chan, one hundred million yen!

126
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:53,960
Ryotsu

127
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,080
Pull yourself together.

128
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:57,400
This is the last chance God has given you!

129
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,480
Save every last yen right now!

130
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,980
That's right, this time,
do what the Chief says

131
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:03,960
and listen, Ryo-chan.

132
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,320
That's right.

133
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,960
Knowing your personality, senpai,

134
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:10,400
if you spend it, it'll be gone in no time.

135
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:14,080
Savings? That word isn't in my dictionary!

136
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:17,160
Idiot! Listen carefully, Ryotsu!

137
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,920
You know the fable of the
ant and the grasshopper, right?

138
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,600
I don't know anything about that.

139
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:24,880
The only thing I know is the Ali
versus Inoki martial arts match.

140
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:30,280
Once upon a time,
there was an ant and a grasshopper.

141
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:36,020
One day, God gave the two of them 100 million yen,
interest-free and with no collateral.

142
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:40,080
Money, money! Now we can have a blast!

143
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:44,720
The grasshopper thought it
was better to play while young.

144
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,440
Let's buy a car,
and I want a motorcycle too.

145
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,440
And then there are overseas trips, too.

146
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:52,680
He spent everything on
leisure and lived happily.

147
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:57,260
Meanwhile, the ant put the 100
million yen into time deposits,

148
00:08:57,260 --> 00:09:00,360
and made steady efforts
to invest and grow it.

149
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:03,300
Before long,
he bought a small plot of land too.

150
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:06,440
"It's my land! Let's build a house here!"

151
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:12,900
Twenty years later, the ant had built his house and grown his savings even more.
One day, he was sitting on a bench

152
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:18,380
when he came across the grasshopper, who had blown through
the 100 million yen and was starving to death on the road.

153
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,860
The end. The end.

154
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,180
That's the story.

155
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:26,260
Now do you understand how
important it is to save money?

156
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:30,320
It was rather obvious in places, but somehow

157
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,020
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

158
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:35,640
But money is meant to be spent, right?

159
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,160
I'm the grasshopper.

160
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:40,320
Stereotypically speaking, fine, I get it.

161
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:45,420
Then this time I'll listen to
the Chief and save every last yen.

162
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,740
That's right. Twenty years from now...

163
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:51,880
the day will come when you'll be
glad you listened to the Chief.

164
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:55,620
But is this really worth 100 million yen?

165
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:58,880
Looks like you need to
see the cash to understand.

166
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:03,760
Wow, this is all real gold!

167
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:06,400
Now, do you get it, Ryotsu?

168
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,340
Senpai!

169
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:10,080
Ryo-chan!

170
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,560
Are you all right, Reiko-san?

171
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,560
Wait, Ryo-chan!

172
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,600
Senpai!

173
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,220
The moment he saw the cash,

174
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:21,880
he went completely feral.

175
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,780
It's like showing dried bonito to a cat.

176
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,440
I've had enough of him.

177
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,960
Go ahead and starve to death on
the road like the grasshopper.

178
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,060
Money, money, money!

179
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:34,060
It's all mine!

180
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,880
Now, what should I do first?

181
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,780
Hey, Pops!
Ten more orders of the top-grade sushi!

182
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:47,620
What should I do next, I wonder?

183
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:49,880
I've got plenty of money, after all.

184
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:56,080
I know! I'll buy some sandals!

185
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,140
That's right, dear.

186
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,840
Ten years' worth of sandals, ma'am!

187
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,800
What are you going to do with that many?

188
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,600
Next up, model kits!

189
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,760
I'll make back what I spent at the races.

190
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:15,240
Race 7, 30 million yen on number 24 to win!

191
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:17,640
Race 8, 20 million yen on the place bet!

192
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:21,620
Race 9, 49,805,000 yen on number 14!

193
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,340
This is the grasshopper's way!

194
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:40,000
What? You've already spent it all?
The whole 100 million yen?

195
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,400
Well, I suppose it's just
what we'd expect from you.

196
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,180
It only took one day, didn't it?

197
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:48,480
After all I said,
you're a complete and utter idiot.

198
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:54,500
Chief, think of it as helping me.
Please lend me 500 yen.

199
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,520
As if I would.

200
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,600
Chief...

201
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:03,280
I wish I could find even
100 yen lying around.

202
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:10,920
What, is the old man just sunbathing?

203
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,740
Are you feeling unwell or something?

204
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:17,600
Hey, what's wrong?

205
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:19,560
Hey, pull yourself together!

206
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,900
Does something hurt?

207
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:24,580
Yeah, I'm a bit dizzy...

208
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:26,380
Honestly, what a pain.

209
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:26,880
Here.

210
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:29,940
I'll take you to the hospital.

211
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:33,140
Honestly, I'm starving too,

212
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:35,280
and now I've picked up
some weird old geezer.

213
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,420
Thanks to you, I already feel much better.

214
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:44,200
I've been getting treated to bread too,
after all.

215
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,720
We're even.

216
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:49,980
Are you a painter?

217
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:50,760
Yes.

218
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:53,020
It's just an old man's hobby.

219
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,060
Well then,

220
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,860
let me take a look.

221
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,520
What is this?

222
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,480
I can't make heads or tails of it, can I?

223
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,840
I hear that a lot.

224
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:09,800
Anyway, it's a terrible painting.
Mine is a hundred times better.

225
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,920
Well, I haven't managed to paint
anything I'm really happy with.

226
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:17,467
Even if I don't look it,
I'm a serialized manga artist.

227
00:13:17,517 --> 00:13:21,380
Robo-Deka Banchō became an anime, you know.
Have you heard of it?

228
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:24,300
Well, I'm not very familiar with that.

229
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,296
I'll teach you how to paint sometime.

230
00:13:26,346 --> 00:13:29,140
You'd be better off starting
over from the basics.

231
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,360
I'm honored. Please, do.

232
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:36,260
So he drew my face for me, but

233
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:37,860
How is it a likeness?

234
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,520
Really, it's worse than the manga!

235
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:44,100
This brushwork looks familiar, doesn't it?

236
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,220
Me too.

237
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,980
This signature.

238
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:50,340
It's Okamoto Bakudan-sensei!

239
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,360
What?

240
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,100
He's a world-famous abstract painter.

241
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:57,940
A Bakudan-sensei painting goes
for tens of millions of yen apiece!

242
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:59,560
A lousy painter like this?

243
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:03,680
Now that you mention it,
this painting does seem artistic.

244
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:04,740
Ryotsu!

245
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,220
No, what on earth did you do?

246
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:09,740
W-what are you talking about?

247
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:12,880
The butler of the Living National Treasure,
Painter Okamoto Bakudan,

248
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:15,360
came to the station asking for you.

249
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:18,580
Did you scribble on the painting
or set fire to the studio?

250
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,320
Just confess quietly.

251
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,880
N-no, that's not it!

252
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:26,580
Senpai found Painter Okamoto
collapsed in the street and helped him.

253
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:27,760
What?

254
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:37,600
Sir, you're from Mr. G's place...
the master, actually, has passed away.

255
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:42,860
How pitiful! That Mr. G...

256
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:59,540
What a shame, he was such a nice old man. My master had no family,
and his estate was to go to those who looked after him before he passed away.

257
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:03,620
The will was written to say
it should be given to Ryo-san.

258
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:05,260
Ryo-chan is getting the inheritance?

259
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:09,660
The late painter Okamoto's
estate must be a huge sum.

260
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:12,620
It's probably no less than 20 billion yen.

261
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,160
W-20 billion?

262
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:18,220
Ryo-chan, listen. This time, no matter what,
you're going to save your money.

263
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,440
W-wait a minute, please.

264
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:23,060
20 billion is too many
digits to even picture.

265
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,740
There are 200 of those cases with
the 100 million yen from before.

266
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,800
All in ten-thousand-yen bills?

267
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,460
Of course, what else would it be?

268
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,440
Wow, that's amazing.

269
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,500
I'm getting dizzy.

270
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:39,060
My blood pressure is, like, really -

271
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:40,200
Are you all right?

272
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:41,840
My master

273
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:45,360
envied Master Ryotsu's
free-spirited way of living.

274
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,220
He said that getting to know Master Ryotsu

275
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:49,920
had truly been a joy.

276
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,040
So,

277
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:54,260
he wants you to use this
inheritance exactly as you please,

278
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,900
to spend every last bit of it.

279
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:57,720
Spend it all.

280
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:00,820
No, stop it!

281
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,920
However, there is a time limit.

282
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,480
Time limit?

283
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,220
It's a condition.

284
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,713
According to your master's will,

285
00:16:08,763 --> 00:16:13,500
if you fail to spend half of it,
10 billion yen, within one week,

286
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:18,060
the entire amount will be
confiscated and donated to a facility.

287
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,940
10 billion yen in one week?

288
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:23,020
W-we're done for.

289
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,120
Me too.

290
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,180
Alright! Got it!

291
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:28,300
W-wait, you understand, Ryo-chan?

292
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:32,040
I'll inherit the estate
and spend every last penny!

293
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:33,460
Are you serious, senpai?

294
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:37,440
It's the old man's wish,
so there's no other choice!

295
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:41,422
Even if we spend 10 billion,
there'll still be 10 billion left.

296
00:16:41,472 --> 00:16:43,400
Is there ever such a sweet deal?

297
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,840
You've said just the right thing.

298
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:49,820
That's the kind of man my master saw in you,
a man among men.

299
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:53,540
This old man will witness
it on my master's behalf.

300
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:55,320
Leave it to me! Alright, let's go!

301
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:02,340
Aaaahh! I'm really a big shot now!

302
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:05,120
I-I-I-Itadakimaaasu!

303
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,040
Me!

304
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:12,560
Me! The top-grade one with gold leaf!

305
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:20,640
Nuhaa! How much was that?
It comes to 118,000 yen, was it?

306
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,200
Aaaaaah!

307
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:33,240
That leaves 9,999,882,000
yen Then add three souvenirs!

308
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:42,320
Nah, I'm just getting started! I bought
up every toy in every toy shop in Tokyo!

309
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,120
You're surprisingly small-time, aren't you?

310
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,740
At this rate,
the late master won't rest in peace.

311
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,700
Alright,
when it comes to what rich people do,

312
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,240
it's a large cruiser!

313
00:17:57,420 --> 00:18:00,580
Move, move!
Even if we crash and sink, we won't die!

314
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:07,000
Drinking champagne while
watching the sun sink.

315
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,300
This is what rich people do!

316
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:14,800
You haven't seen anything yet.

317
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:19,140
As everyone knows,
what rich people tend to do is

318
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:21,880
the other day, Okamoto dropped a bombshell.

319
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:26,420
A police officer who inherited a massive
fortune has started doing something outrageous.

320
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,220
He's building a private railway all the way

321
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:33,600
from his bachelor dorm to
his workplace police box.

322
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:38,080
Ryo-san, are you really planning
to run a train through here?

323
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:41,500
We're also rebuilding Nikoniko
Dorm into a deluxe version!

324
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,140
It's called the Gorgeous Nikoniko Dorm!

325
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:47,260
This Cinderella cop, Mr. Ryotsu,

326
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:50,100
bought every seat in Tokyo
Dome for himself today.

327
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,400
He reportedly plans to
watch a baseball game.

328
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,840
Nice one, Matsui!

329
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:04,780
Hehehehehe

330
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,060
Yotsu-sama

331
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:09,380
I am very disappointed.

332
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:13,140
Four days have passed since you
inherited the master's estate,

333
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,420
and you haven't even
spent 5 billion yen yet.

334
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:20,200
You had the Iron Chef make your snacks,

335
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,088
and during your nap, Morning Musume.

336
00:19:22,138 --> 00:19:24,400
sang you lullabies live, and so on,

337
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,320
but it's not going down very fast, is it.

338
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:32,720
At this rate,
the master must be lamenting from his grave.

339
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,320
Okay, okay, I get it.

340
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:37,820
Alright, let's hit Ginza after
this and blow through it quickly.

341
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:39,720
That's not allowed.

342
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:44,360
The master's orders were that it must not be thrown away,
buried, or burned.

343
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:47,920
You have to use up everything
that's left within three days.

344
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:52,740
Spending money is harder than I thought.

345
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,540
Something under the chair...
what the heck is this?

346
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,520
It's a jewel!

347
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:01,060
There it is, over there!

348
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:05,880
Baghdad, Sinbad, Ocean Blood!

349
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,440
What?!

350
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:10,480
That jewel was lost by this man.

351
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:12,620
It's worth several tens
of billions on the market.

352
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:15,080
He says he'll give you
ten percent as a thank-you.

353
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:16,540
W-what?

354
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:19,800
I said I didn't want it!

355
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:22,780
Now it's grown by a whole truckload.

356
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:24,540
Ryo-san's...

357
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:26,080
I know, I know.

358
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:29,800
Alright,
next we're renting out all of Tokyo Ratland!

359
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:41,120
We can ride the Ninja attractions that
usually have two-hour lines hundreds of times!

360
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:48,800
Even if we could ride along...

361
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:53,000
Yes, yes, here you go, here you go.

362
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:57,840
As long as you've got the money,
you can scribble all the graffiti you want!

363
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:00,580
How about it?

364
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:03,720
Wonderful!

365
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:06,420
This is exactly the character
I've been looking for!

366
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:07,800
What is this?

367
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,780
I'm Walt Mazumi.

368
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,120
Please, let us use this picture!

369
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:15,300
We'll pay 10 billion yen
as a character usage fee.

370
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:19,640
I already told you, I don't want it!

371
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,840
Damn it, another one's been added!

372
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:24,420
Father.

373
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:27,540
Our late master would
surely have been delighted.

374
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,080
If it's come to this, then it's the horses.

375
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:37,020
I'll bet 30 billion yen
on some worthless horse.

376
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,560
Hey, miss!

377
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:39,080
Yes?

378
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:43,060
30 billion yen to win
on Thunder Dung Roller!

379
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,860
200 meters left in the straightaway.

380
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:47,640
Eijin Hayate is still leading at the front!

381
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:50,400
Rising Bull, the second favorite,
is making its way up on the outside!

382
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,800
The top favorite,
Thunder Dung Roller, has frozen up!

383
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:53,560
Left and right!

384
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:55,460
The popular Side Binder is coming too!

385
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,320
A fierce head-to-head battle!

386
00:21:58,300 --> 00:22:01,480
Then Side Binder, which had been in front,
swerves and makes contact with Eijin Hayate!

387
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:04,980
Two horses have fallen! Rising Bull, coming
up on the outside, is caught up in it too!

388
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:08,560
The horses right behind them are
getting caught up one after another!

389
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:10,860
The favorites and their challengers
are falling off one after another!

390
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:14,380
Somehow, Thunder Dung Roller,
now the top favorite, takes first place!

391
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:16,160
Why?!

392
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:37,060
This is bad for my health.

393
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:42,100
Why does it keep growing when
I'm trying to cut it down?

394
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:47,660
I have to spend all 10
billion yen by tomorrow!

395
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:52,860
That's it, if it's come to this,
I'm done spending!

396
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:55,760
Let's take this money and flee overseas.

397
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:06,780
I've already taken out all the money.

398
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:09,380
Finally, I'm free of that old man!

399
00:23:10,460 --> 00:23:11,740
Right, I'll save it!

400
00:23:11,740 --> 00:23:13,200
If I save this much,

401
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:14,980
I can live in luxury for the rest
of my life on the interest alone,

402
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,020
and live a fun, carefree life!

403
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:20,880
What's that bell for?

404
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,660
I'm sorry, Master Ryotsu.

405
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:25,460
Time's up.

406
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:26,380
What?

407
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:31,600
Ryo-sama, press it! Boop!

408
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:34,840
That's ridiculous!

409
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:39,680
So, where's Ryo-chan?

410
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:43,420
Nobody knows where it fell. It's missing.

411
00:23:43,420 --> 00:23:46,480
He ran off with the money,
so he got what was coming to him.

412
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,880
Serves him right.

413
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:55,920
I'm hungry.

414
00:23:57,220 --> 00:24:00,560
I don't want money.
Just give me something to eat.

415
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:45,380
I tried walking only on the black parts.

416
00:24:47,940 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone's forgotten.

417
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,680
Politicians with their self-important faces,

418
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:00,980
and aunties with blue eyeshadow, too.

419
00:25:00,980 --> 00:25:06,600
Try turning at that corner.

420
00:25:07,820 --> 00:25:11,800
You can meet everyone, everyone.

421
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:16,220
That's Kameari over there.

422
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:19,660
It's surely Kameari.

423
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:24,900
Everyone, come to our town!

424
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:26,540
Thank you.

425
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:32,060
What? A TV crew is doing an
exclusive feature on the police box?

426
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,700
Those old ladies of the old town,
well, that's...

427
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,360
Isn't this the place where they grill the
"otsuroi"?

428
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:41,140
Alright, my cool working self!

429
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:43,540
We're going to broadcast it nationwide!

430
00:25:43,540 --> 00:25:48,140
Next time, Burari's close-up on the North Town officers,
see you then!

431
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,820
That's Kameari over there.

432
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:54,160
Well, surely it's Kameari.

433
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:59,280
Everyone, come to our town!

434
00:26:00,380 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

